<title>INDIA: India lower house approves ex-im bank capital hike.</title>
<headline>India lower house approves ex-im bank capital hike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's lower house (Lok Sabha) of parliament on Wednesday approved a bill raising the authorised capital of the state-run Export-Import Bank of India to 10 billion rupees ($280 million) from five billion.</p>
<p>The legislation also provides for enhancing the bank's authorised capital to up to 20 billion rupees, if required, through a notification.</p>
<p>Moving the Export-Import Bank of India (amendment) Bill, 1997, Finance Minister P. Chidambaram assured parliament deputies that his ministry will ask the bank to consider extending facilities to small industries. ($1 = 35.7 rupees)</p>
</text>
